## File Organization

### SCSS Structure

```
scss/
├── app.scss                 # Main entry point
├── reset.scss              # CSS reset
├── variables.scss          # Global variables
├── MaterialTheme/
│   ├── index.ts           # Theme configuration
│   ├── typography.ts      # Typography scale
│   ├── shadow.ts          # Shadow system
│   └── styled.ts          # Styled components
├── pc/
│   ├── main.scss          # PC main styles
│   ├── general.scss       # PC general styles
│   └── [feature]/         # Feature-specific styles
└── mobile/
    ├── main.scss          # Mobile main styles
    └── general.scss       # Mobile general styles
```

### Import Order

```scss
@import 'variables.scss';
@import 'reset.scss';
```

---

## Best Practices

### 1. Naming Conventions
- Use kebab-case for class names: `.property-card`, `.user-info`
- Use semantic names: `.card-wrapper` not `.box1`
- Prefix page-specific IDs: `#property-list-page`, `#my-page`

### 2. Specificity
- Avoid deep nesting (max 3-4 levels)
- Use direct child selectors when appropriate
- Avoid `!important` unless absolutely necessary

### 3. Reusability
- Extract common patterns into reusable classes
- Use consistent spacing values
- Maintain DRY principles

### 4. Performance
- Minimize use of expensive properties (box-shadow, filter)
- Use `transform` for animations (GPU-accelerated)
- Optimize selector specificity

### 5. Accessibility
- Maintain color contrast ratios (WCAG AA minimum)
- Use appropriate font sizes (minimum 12px)
- Ensure interactive elements are adequately sized

### 6. Consistency
- Follow the established spacing scale
- Use defined border-radius values
- Stick to the typography scale
- Use standard transition timings

